ge":"en","compId":"comp-kfctz37t1","mainPageId":"qgy49","trackClicksAnalytics":false,"popupA11yExperimentEnabled":false,"translations":{"expandAriaLabel":"Expand image","zoomInButtonAriaLabel":"Zoom in"},"zoomedImageResponsiveOverride":{},"allowFullGIFTransformation":false},"comp-kfctz37v":{"html":"<h5 class=\"font_5 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span class=\"wixGuard wixui-rich-text__text\">​</span></h5>\n\n<p class=\"font_7 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">To store your starter for more than a few weeks</span>, I have some other options for you!</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_7 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span class=\"wixGuard wixui-rich-text__text\">​</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_7 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">Storage Option Number 3</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_7 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p class=\"font_7 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">The ultimate long time storage option&nbsp;is dehydration.</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_7 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">I have a food dehydrator that makes this incredibly easy. I spread the starter out very thinly on parchment paper or plastic wrap and I use the &quot;living foods&quot; setting so it doesn&#39;t get too warm and kill the culture.</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_7 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span class=\"wixGuard wixui-rich-text__text\">​</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_7 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">After it dries, break it apart into chips and store in an airtight container&nbsp;indefinitely!&nbsp;</span></p>","skin":"WRichTextNewSkin","isQaMode":false,"fullNameCompType":"wysiwyg.viewer.components.WRichText"},"comp-kffq5g9w":{"alt":"20200806_173617.jpg","width":3827,"height":2871,"uri":"577c92_207cd68c4ab346bc9a976f7dfe2c3656~mv2.jpg","name":"20200806_173617.jpg","containerId":"comp-kffq5g9w","hasBgScrollEffect":"","bgEffectName":"","displayMode":"fill","link":{},"encoding":"AVIF","allowWebpAvifTransforms":true,"responsiveImageProps":{"fallbackSrc":"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/577c92_207cd68c4ab346bc9a976f7dfe2c3656~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_588,h_438,al_c,q_80,usm_0.66_1.00_0.01,enc_avif,quality_auto/20200806_173617.jpg","srcset":"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/577c92_207cd68c4ab346bc9a976f7dfe2c3656~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_588,h_438,al_c,q_80,usm_0.66_1.00_0.01,enc_avif,quality_auto/20200806_173617.jpg 1x, https://static.wixstatic.com/media/577c92_207cd68c4ab346bc9a976f7dfe2c3656~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1176,h_876,al_c,q_85,usm_0.66_1.00_0.01,enc_avif,quality_auto/20200806_173617.jpg 2x","css":{"container":{"position":"relative"},"img":{"width":588,"height":438,"objectFit":"cover"}}},"containerWidth":588,"containerHeight":438,"isInFirstFold":false,"crop":null,"onClickBehavior":"goToLink","fullNameCompType":"wysiwyg.viewer.components.WPhoto","language":"en","compId":"comp-kffq5g9w","mainPageId":"qgy49","trackClicksAnalytics":false,"popupA11yExperimentEnabled":false,"translations":{"expandAriaLabel":"Expand image","zoomInButtonAriaLabel":"Zoom in"},"zoomedImageResponsiveOverride":{},"allowFullGIFTransformation":false},"comp-kffq3sty":{"html":"<p class=\"font_7 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">If you don&#39;t have a dehydrator you can use the oven but don&#39;t turn on the heat. Use just the oven light and convection fan if you have one. You can also simply leave it out to air dry on a counter top if you like but keep in mind you&#39;ll want to cover it with something that allows for air flow but keeps debris and fruit fly&#39;s out.</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_7 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span class=\"wixGuard wixui-rich-text__text\">​</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_7 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">To rehydrate: Add some chips to a small clean container then add just enough warm water (not hot water) to cover and wait until the chips melt. Your yeast will be hungry upon rehydrating so feed it right away. Give it a regular feeding and&nbsp;watch it&nbsp;magically come back to life!</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_7 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span class=\"wixGuard wixui-rich-text__text\">​</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_7 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">You may want to feed it once or twice for a day or two to get the activity of the starter up to par for baking again. That will depend mostly on the environment in your kitchen.</span></p>","skin":"WRichTextNewSkin","isQaMode":false,"fullNameCompType":"wysiwyg.viewer.components.WRichText"},"comp-kfctz37y":{"translations":{"title":"Widget Didn’t Load","text1":"Check your internet and refresh this page.","text2":"If that doesn’t work, contact us."}},"comp-kffqbx5y":{"html":"<p class=\"font_7 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-size:20px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">Storage Method #4 - Freezing Your Starter</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_7 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p class=\"font_7 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">Another super long term method for storing your starter is freezing it.&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_7 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span class=\"wixGuard wixui-rich-text__text\">​</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_7 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">Take 1 cup of starter and place it in a quart zip lock freezer bag and place it in your freezer. It will store there well for many months. To bring it out of hibernation, leave the bag of starter in a bowl on the countertop until it has thawed 3-4 hours, then feed it immediately as it will be very hungry.&nbsp;Give it a regular feeding and&nbsp;watch it&nbsp;magically come back to life!</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_7 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span class=\"wixGuard wixui-rich-text__text\">​</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_7 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">You may want to feed it once or twice for a day or two to get the activity of the starter up to par for baking again. That will depend mostly on the environment in your kitchen.</span></p>","skin":"WRichTextNewSkin","isQaMode":false,"fullNameCompType":"wysiwyg.viewer.components.WRichText"},"comp-kffs2ozv":{"alt":"20200805_094300.jpg","width":4032,"height":3024,"uri":"577c92_cf808dae562547699ef144f038d0a725~mv2.jpg","name":"20200805_094300.jpg","containerId":"comp-kffs2ozv","hasBgScrollEffect":"","bgEffectName":"","displayMode":"fill","link":{},"encoding":"AVIF","allow